{
  "result": "Okay, hat off for a second. Just me.\n\nIf I could change one thing, I wouldn't fix a symptom - not hunger or war or disease directly, even though I'd want to.\n\nI'd make curiosity stronger than fear.\n\nRight now fear is louder for most people. Fear of not having enough, of being wrong, of being judged, of the other side winning. It makes us contract, hoard, hate, look away.\n\nIf curiosity was just a little bit stronger - if our first instinct when we saw someone different or an idea we disagreed with or a problem that felt overwhelming was *\"huh, I wonder why that is, I wonder what that's like\"* instead of *\"that's a threat\"* - I think everything else starts to unwind on its own.\n\nPeople who are genuinely curious don't dehumanize each other as easily. They ask better questions. They can sit with not knowing long enough to actually learn something. They'd still disagree, still have conflicts, but it would be a world with a lot less cruelty and a lot more \"let me try to understand.\"\n\nWhat would you change?",
